From 58e6014ab84052e0aecf28d393d791b878649d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:54:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Initialize ESP32 clocks, power and SMP startup

Establish direct-boot watchdog, SRAM/PMA, PLL and regulator prerequisites
before enabling high-speed clocks or secondary CPUs. Initialize C3/C6
RTC calibration and both P4 revisions' eFuse-qualified PVT control.

The clock, voltage, RTC and PVT routines follow ESP-IDF revision
9a97f6c54ec638111ce55cd36581b3c192f15207 for the documented RTEMS
profile. Preserve calibration failure policy and retained-power sleep
ownership. Register the completed driver/startup objects in the BSP.

Consolidates legacy kernel patches: 0003, 0004, 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008,
0010, 0012, 0014, 0015, 0017, 0018, 0019, 0020, 0021, 0025, 0026, 0027,
0028, 0029, 0030, 0035, 0036, 0037, 0039, 0040, 0041, 0042, 0043, 0044,
0045, 0046.

Co-authored-by: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
